{"cells":[{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"e9863c14","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.002971,"end_time":"2026-11-25T21:56:21.35454+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-25T21:56:21.351569+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["# Notebook 05 · Diseño de la arquitectura del modelo\n","\n","**Proyecto #7 · Módulo de latidos (extrasístoles ventriculares)**\n","\n","Aquí presento la decisión de qué capas tiene, qué hace cada una y cuántos parámetros guarda, y se comprueba que cabe en el Arduino Nano 33 BLE Sense (1 MB de flash, 256 KB de RAM).\n","\n","| Pregunta | Mi decisión | Por qué |\n","|---|---|---|\n","| ¿Para qué módulo? | **Clasificador de latidos** | Una red convolucional reconoce la **forma** de la señal (QRS ancho = extrasístole ventricular). El módulo de FA ya funciona con medidas de R–R |\n","| ¿Qué entra? | **Un latido**: 0.25 s antes y 0.40 s después del pico R, a 360 Hz = **234 muestras** | Incluye la onda P, el QRS y la onda T; es la misma ventana del notebook de latidos |\n","| ¿Qué sale? | **3 clases AAMI: N (normal), S (supraventricular), V (ventricular)** | V es la que pide mi proyecto; S se incluye porque también llega antes de tiempo y el modelo debe aprender a no confundirlas |\n","| ¿Basada en cuál? | **DS-CNN** (convoluciones separables en profundidad) | Hace el mismo trabajo que una CNN 1D con **varias veces menos parámetros**: ideal para un microcontrolador (Zhang et al., 2017; Loroch et al., 2025) |\n","| ¿Cuántas capas? | **5** | Para empezar desde lo simple |"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"e0edcf1c","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.002243,"end_time":"2026-11-25T21:56:21.359214+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-25T21:56:21.356971+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["## Preparación\n","\n","La parte de **cálculo** (secciones 1 a 3) solo usa `numpy` y funciona en cualquier lado. La parte de **TensorFlow** (secciones 4 y 5) se corre mejor en **Kaggle**, que ya lo trae instalado. Si no está, esas celdas avisan y se saltan."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":1,"id":"c65cb991","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-25T21:56:21.365313Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-25T21:56:21.364989Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-25T21:56:41.88609Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-25T21:56:41.884892Z"},"papermill":{"duration":20.526768,"end_time":"2026-11-25T21:56:41.888136+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-25T21:56:21.361368+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"name":"stderr","output_type":"stream","text":["WARNING: All log messages before absl::InitializeLog() is called are written to STDERR\n","I0000 00:00:1795643783.936489      16 cudart_stub.cc:31] Could not find cuda drivers on your machine, GPU will not be used.\n","WARNING: All log messages before absl::InitializeLog() is called are written to STDERR\n","I0000 00:00:1795643798.055480      16 cudart_stub.cc:31] Could not find cuda drivers on your machine, GPU will not be used.\n"]},{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["TensorFlow 2.21.0 disponible\n"]}],"source":["import numpy as np\n","import pandas as pd\n","import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n","from matplotlib.patches import FancyBboxPatch\n","from IPython.display import display\n","\n","try:\n","    import tensorflow as tf\n","    HAY_TF = True\n","    print(\"TensorFlow\", tf.__version__, \"disponible\")\n","except ImportError:\n","    HAY_TF = False\n","    print(\"TensorFlow no está instalado: las secciones 4 y 5 se saltarán (córrelas en Kaggle)\")"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"bef0b4f5","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.002313,"end_time":"2026-11-25T21:56:41.892946+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-25T21:56:41.890633+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["## 1. Decisiones de la arquitectura\n"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":2,"id":"f4852847","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-25T21:56:41.899965Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-25T21:56:41.898866Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-25T21:56:41.906494Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-25T21:56:41.905407Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.013163,"end_time":"2026-11-25T21:56:41.908395+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-25T21:56:41.895232+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["Entrada: 234 muestras (0.65 s) · Salida: 3 clases ['N', 'S', 'V']\n"]}],"source":["FS = 360                         # muestras por segundo (igual que MIT-BIH y el Arduino)\n","ANTES_S, DESPUES_S = 0.25, 0.40  # ventana del latido alrededor del pico R\n","LARGO = int(ANTES_S * FS) + int(DESPUES_S * FS)   # 90 + 144 = 234 muestras\n","CLASES = [\"N\", \"S\", \"V\"]\n","\n","# Capa 1: convolución normal\n","FILTROS_1, KERNEL_1 = 8, 7\n","# Capas 2 y 3: convoluciones separables en profundidad\n","FILTROS_2, KERNEL_2 = 16, 5\n","FILTROS_3, KERNEL_3 = 32, 5\n","POOL = 2                         # cada bloque reduce el largo a la mitad\n","\n","print(f\"Entrada: {LARGO} muestras ({LARGO / FS:.2f} s) · Salida: {len(CLASES)} clases {CLASES}\")"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"b2523abe","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.002322,"end_time":"2026-11-25T21:56:41.913287+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-25T21:56:41.910965+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["---\n","## 2. La arquitectura, capa por capa\n","\n","```\n","Latido (234 muestras, 1 canal)\n","   │\n","   ▼  CAPA 1 · Conv1D normal (8 filtros de 7)        → busca formas simples: subidas, bajadas, picos\n","   ▼          + MaxPooling (÷2)                       → resume: se queda con lo más fuerte de cada par\n","   ▼  CAPA 2 · Conv1D separable (16 filtros de 5)    → combina formas simples en formas medianas (QRS, onda T)\n","   ▼          + MaxPooling (÷2)\n","   ▼  CAPA 3 · Conv1D separable (32 filtros de 5)    → combina en formas complejas (\"QRS ancho sin P\")\n","   ▼          + MaxPooling (÷2)\n","   ▼  CAPA 4 · Global Average Pooling                → resume cada filtro en UN número (¿cuánto apareció su forma?)\n","   ▼  CAPA 5 · Dense + softmax                        → decide: probabilidad de N, S y V\n","   │\n","   ▼\n","\"Este latido es V con 92 % de probabilidad\"\n","```\n","\n","### ¿Cómo se cuentan los parámetros?\n","\n","| Tipo de capa | Fórmula | Qué es cada letra |\n","|---|---|---|\n","| **Conv1D normal** | k × C_ent × C_sal + C_sal | k = tamaño del filtro, C_ent = canales que entran, C_sal = filtros (canales que salen). El último término son los *sesgos* (uno por filtro) |\n","| **Conv1D separable** | k × C_ent  +  C_ent × C_sal  +  C_sal | **Paso 1, depthwise:** un filtro de tamaño k por cada canal (k × C_ent). **Paso 2, pointwise:** mezcla los canales (C_ent × C_sal). Más los sesgos |\n","| **Pooling (Max o Global Average)** | 0 | Solo resume (elige el máximo o saca el promedio); no aprende nada |\n","| **Dense** | entradas × salidas + salidas | Cada salida se conecta con todas las entradas |\n","\n","### Detalle de cada capa\n","\n","**CAPA 1 · Conv1D normal (8 filtros, tamaño 7) + MaxPooling.**\n","*Función:* 8 \"lupas\" de 7 muestras (~19 ms) recorren el latido y cada una aprende a detectar una forma simple (una subida rápida, un pico, una bajada).\n","*¿Por qué normal y no separable?* La entrada tiene **un solo canal**: separarla no ahorra nada. Así lo hacen también las DS-CNN de la literatura (Zhang et al., 2017).\n","*Parámetros:* 7 × 1 × 8 + 8 = **64**.\n","*MaxPooling:* de cada 2 muestras se queda con la mayor. El latido pasa de 234 a 117 posiciones. 0 parámetros.\n","\n","**CAPA 2 · Conv1D separable (16 filtros, tamaño 5) + MaxPooling.**\n","*Función:* combina las 8 formas simples en 16 formas más complejas (por ejemplo, \"subida + bajada rápida\" = QRS).\n","*Parámetros:* depthwise 5 × 8 = 40, pointwise 8 × 16 = 128, sesgos 16 → **184**. (Una Conv1D normal necesitaría 5 × 8 × 16 + 16 = 656.)\n","\n","**CAPA 3 · Conv1D separable (32 filtros, tamaño 5) + MaxPooling.**\n","*Función:* combina en 32 formas complejas, como \"QRS ancho\", \"onda T invertida\" o \"no hay onda P\".\n","*Parámetros:* depthwise 5 × 16 = 80, pointwise 16 × 32 = 512, sesgos 32 → **624**. (Normal: 5 × 16 × 32 + 32 = 2,592.)\n","\n","**CAPA 4 · Global Average Pooling.**\n","*Función:* cada uno de los 32 filtros se resume en **un solo número**: el promedio de cuánto apareció su forma a lo largo del latido. Queda una lista de 32 números.\n","*Parámetros:* **0**.\n","\n","**CAPA 5 · Dense con softmax (3 salidas).**\n","*Función:* con esos 32 números decide el tipo de latido. *Softmax* convierte el resultado en **probabilidades** que suman 1 (por ejemplo N = 0.05, S = 0.03, V = 0.92).\n","*Parámetros:* 32 × 3 + 3 = **99**.\n","\n","Las capas convolucionales usan la activación **ReLU** (deja pasar los valores positivos y pone en 0 los negativos), que es simple y está soportada en TFLite Micro."]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"7e6ae4c7","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.002646,"end_time":"2026-11-25T21:56:41.918275+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-25T21:56:41.915629+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["---\n","## 3. Cálculo automático de parámetros, memoria y operaciones\n","\n","Esta celda calcula, para cada capa: el tamaño de lo que sale, los parámetros, la memoria en el Arduino y las operaciones (multiplicaciones). Además calcula la misma red con **convoluciones normales** (una CNN 1D) para comparar.\n","\n","- **Flash (pesos):** con cuantización INT8 cada parámetro ocupa **1 byte**.\n","- **RAM (activaciones):** mientras el Arduino calcula una capa, necesita guardar **lo que entra y lo que sale** de esa capa (1 byte por valor en INT8). Lo que importa es el **pico**: la capa que más RAM ocupa.\n","- **MACs:** multiplicaciones y sumas por latido. Sirven para estimar el tiempo de cálculo."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":3,"id":"8d8e8a06","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-25T21:56:41.925375Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-25T21:56:41.924422Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-25T21:56:41.963627Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-25T21:56:41.962844Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.045038,"end_time":"2026-11-25T21:56:41.965674+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-25T21:56:41.920636+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"data":{"text/html":["<div>\n","<style scoped>\n","    .dataframe tbody tr th:only-of-type {\n","        vertical-align: middle;\n","    }\n","\n","    .dataframe tbody tr th {\n","        vertical-align: top;\n","    }\n","\n","    .dataframe thead th {\n","        text-align: right;\n","    }\n","</style>\n","<table border=\"1\" class=\"dataframe\">\n","  <thead>\n","    <tr style=\"text-align: right;\">\n","      <th></th>\n","      <th>capa</th>\n","      <th>tipo</th>\n","      <th>salida</th>\n","      <th>parámetros</th>\n","      <th>flash INT8 (bytes)</th>\n","      <th>RAM pico (bytes)</th>\n","      <th>MACs</th>\n","    </tr>\n","  </thead>\n","  <tbody>\n","    <tr>\n","      <th>0</th>\n","      <td>1 · Conv1D</td>\n","      <td>normal</td>\n","      <td>234 × 8</td>\n","      <td>64</td>\n","      <td>64</td>\n","      <td>2106</td>\n","      <td>13104</td>\n","    </tr>\n","    <tr>\n","      <th>1</th>\n","      <td>MaxPooling</td>\n","      <td>pooling</td>\n","      <td>117 × 8</td>\n","      <td>0</td>\n","      <td>0</td>\n","      <td>2808</td>\n","      <td>0</td>\n","    </tr>\n","    <tr>\n","      <th>2</th>\n","      <td>2 · SeparableConv1D</td>\n","      <td>separable</td>\n","      <td>117 × 16</td>\n","      <td>184</td>\n","      <td>184</td>\n","      <td>3744</td>\n","      <td>19656</td>\n","    </tr>\n","    <tr>\n","      <th>3</th>\n","      <td>MaxPooling</td>\n","      <td>pooling</td>\n","      <td>58 × 16</td>\n","      <td>0</td>\n","      <td>0</td>\n","      <td>2800</td>\n","      <td>0</td>\n","    </tr>\n","    <tr>\n","      <th>4</th>\n","      <td>3 · SeparableConv1D</td>\n","      <td>separable</td>\n","      <td>58 × 32</td>\n","      <td>624</td>\n","      <td>624</td>\n","      <td>3712</td>\n","      <td>34336</td>\n","    </tr>\n","    <tr>\n","      <th>5</th>\n","      <td>MaxPooling</td>\n","      <td>pooling</td>\n","      <td>29 × 32</td>\n","      <td>0</td>\n","      <td>0</td>\n","      <td>2784</td>\n","      <td>0</td>\n","    </tr>\n","    <tr>\n","      <th>6</th>\n","      <td>4 · GlobalAveragePooling</td>\n","      <td>pooling</td>\n","      <td>1 × 32</td>\n","      <td>0</td>\n","      <td>0</td>\n","      <td>960</td>\n","      <td>0</td>\n","    </tr>\n","    <tr>\n","      <th>7</th>\n","      <td>5 · Dense (softmax)</td>\n","      <td>densa</td>\n","      <td>1 × 3</td>\n","      <td>99</td>\n","      <td>99</td>\n","      <td>931</td>\n","      <td>96</td>\n","    </tr>\n","  </tbody>\n","</table>\n","</div>"],"text/plain":["                       capa       tipo    salida  parámetros  \\\n","0                1 · Conv1D     normal   234 × 8          64   \n","1                MaxPooling    pooling   117 × 8           0   \n","2       2 · SeparableConv1D  separable  117 × 16         184   \n","3                MaxPooling    pooling   58 × 16           0   \n","4       3 · SeparableConv1D  separable   58 × 32         624   \n","5                MaxPooling    pooling   29 × 32           0   \n","6  4 · GlobalAveragePooling    pooling    1 × 32           0   \n","7       5 · Dense (softmax)      densa     1 × 3          99   \n","\n","   flash INT8 (bytes)  RAM pico (bytes)   MACs  \n","0                  64              2106  13104  \n","1                   0              2808      0  \n","2                 184              3744  19656  \n","3                   0              2800      0  \n","4                 624              3712  34336  \n","5                   0              2784      0  \n","6                   0               960      0  \n","7                  99               931     96  "]},"metadata":{},"output_type":"display_data"},{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["\n","TOTAL DS-CNN:  971 parámetros  ·  pesos ≈ 0.95 KB (INT8)  ·  RAM pico ≈ 3.66 KB  ·  67,192 MACs por latido\n"]}],"source":["def calcular_capas(separable=True):\n","    filas, largo, canales = [], LARGO, 1\n","\n","    def agregar(nombre, tipo, params, largo_sal, canales_sal, macs, ram_extra=0):\n","        filas.append({\"capa\": nombre, \"tipo\": tipo, \"salida\": f\"{largo_sal} × {canales_sal}\",\n","                      \"parámetros\": params, \"flash INT8 (bytes)\": params,\n","                      \"RAM pico (bytes)\": largo * canales + largo_sal * canales_sal + ram_extra,\n","                      \"MACs\": macs})\n","\n","    # Capa 1: Conv1D normal (padding 'same': el largo no cambia) + MaxPooling\n","    p = KERNEL_1 * canales * FILTROS_1 + FILTROS_1\n","    agregar(\"1 · Conv1D\", \"normal\", p, largo, FILTROS_1, largo * KERNEL_1 * canales * FILTROS_1)\n","    canales = FILTROS_1\n","    agregar(\"    MaxPooling\", \"pooling\", 0, largo // POOL, canales, 0)\n","    largo //= POOL\n","\n","    # Capas 2 y 3: Conv1D separable (o normal, para comparar) + MaxPooling\n","    for n, (filtros, k) in enumerate([(FILTROS_2, KERNEL_2), (FILTROS_3, KERNEL_3)], start=2):\n","        if separable:\n","            p = k * canales + canales * filtros + filtros\n","            macs = largo * k * canales + largo * canales * filtros\n","            agregar(f\"{n} · SeparableConv1D\", \"separable\", p, largo, filtros, macs, ram_extra=largo * canales)\n","        else:\n","            p = k * canales * filtros + filtros\n","            agregar(f\"{n} · Conv1D\", \"normal\", p, largo, filtros, largo * k * canales * filtros)\n","        canales = filtros\n","        agregar(\"    MaxPooling\", \"pooling\", 0, largo // POOL, canales, 0)\n","        largo //= POOL\n","\n","    # Capa 4: Global Average Pooling\n","    agregar(\"4 · GlobalAveragePooling\", \"pooling\", 0, 1, canales, 0)\n","    # Capa 5: Dense + softmax\n","    agregar(\"5 · Dense (softmax)\", \"densa\", canales * len(CLASES) + len(CLASES), 1, len(CLASES),\n","            canales * len(CLASES))\n","    return pd.DataFrame(filas)\n","\n","tabla_ds = calcular_capas(separable=True)\n","tabla_cnn = calcular_capas(separable=False)\n","display(tabla_ds)\n","\n","total_params = int(tabla_ds[\"parámetros\"].sum())\n","ram_pico = int(tabla_ds[\"RAM pico (bytes)\"].max())\n","total_macs = int(tabla_ds[\"MACs\"].sum())\n","print(f\"\\nTOTAL DS-CNN:  {total_params:,} parámetros  ·  pesos ≈ {total_params / 1024:.2f} KB (INT8)\"\n","      f\"  ·  RAM pico ≈ {ram_pico / 1024:.2f} KB  ·  {total_macs:,} MACs por latido\")"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"fd1b1513","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.00261,"end_time":"2026-11-25T21:56:41.97103+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-25T21:56:41.96842+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["\n","\n","### 3.1 ¿Cabe en el Arduino?"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":4,"id":"3b64a497","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-25T21:56:41.977589Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-25T21:56:41.977281Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-25T21:56:41.982953Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-25T21:56:41.982082Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.011222,"end_time":"2026-11-25T21:56:41.984766+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-25T21:56:41.973544+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["Pesos:              0.95 KB  de 1024 KB de flash (0.09 %)\n","Activaciones:       3.66 KB  de 256 KB de RAM (1.43 %)\n","Tiempo estimado:  ~1.0 ms por latido a 64 MHz (estimación gruesa; se medirá en el Arduino). Meta del proyecto: < 200 ms\n"]}],"source":["FLASH_ARDUINO, RAM_ARDUINO = 1024 * 1024, 256 * 1024\n","# El archivo .tflite real pesa algo más que los puros pesos (guarda la estructura de la red);\n","# en la literatura, modelos de este tamaño ocupan unos pocos KB extra.\n","print(f\"Pesos:            {total_para